show ip dhcp binding

Check DHCP-assigned addresses.

show ip dhcp pool

Check DHCP pools.

show ip nat translations

Check active NAT/PAT translations.

show ip nat statistics

Check NAT inside/outside interfaces and statistics.

ping 10.0.0.5

Test DHCP Router → ISP Router connectivity.

🧠 What I Learned From This Lab

The main things practiced in this setup were:

1. Router-on-a-Stick

One physical router interface can handle multiple VLANs using subinterfaces.

Fa0/0
 ├── Fa0/0.10 → VLAN 10
 ├── Fa0/0.20 → VLAN 20
 ├── Fa0/0.30 → VLAN 30
 └── Fa0/0.70 → VLAN 70
2. DHCP on a Router

The router can dynamically assign:

IP Address
Subnet Mask
Default Gateway

to clients in different VLANs.

3. Static Routing

The DHCP Router uses:

0.0.0.0/0 → 10.0.0.5

while the ISP Router uses:

192.168.x.0/24 → 10.0.0.6
4. NAT

Internal private addresses are translated when going toward the WAN.

192.168.x.x
     ↓
   NAT
     ↓
10.0.0.6
5. PAT

Multiple clients can share one outside address:

PC1 ─┐
PC2 ─┤
PC3 ─┼──> PAT ──> 10.0.0.6
PC4 ─┘
6. End-to-End Routing

Successfully tested:

